HostMot2 PktUART software regression tests
========================================

Compiles the production driver with mock LLIO. No hardware is accessed.
Run after configuring/building a run-in-place tree:

    scripts/rip-environment runtests tests/hostmot2/pktuart
    SANITIZERS=address,undefined bash tests/hostmot2/pktuart/test.sh

CC can select another C compiler. Sanitizers are optional.
Checks cover queue counts, high-bit byte packing, missing/unconfigured
instances, zero and negative LLIO failures at each transfer stage, failed
configuration retries, legacy setup, and reset diagnostics.

A successful queue operation is not confirmation that hardware received it.
On a partial queue failure, earlier operations may remain queued; callers
must handle the error and recover, not blindly resend the entire request.

Hardware validation remains pending: record commit hash, board/firmware,
configuration, and results for hm2_modbus traffic, multi-frame transfers,
empty/full FIFO behavior, configuration changes and connection recovery.
